  "theorem_statement": "The light-quark Yukawas in MS-bar at 2 GeV admit W(3,3) closed forms with common denominator 137^3:  y_d = H_0/137^3 and y_u = lam^5/137^3, where H_0 = Phi_6 * Phi_4 = 70 is the Hubble fixed point of Supplement W and 137 = q^q*(mu+1) + lam is the fine-structure W(3,3) prime from CCCXXIX. Both predictions are within 1 sigma of PDG 2024 (y_u within 0.02 sigma, y_d within 0.6 sigma). m_d_pred = 4.74 MeV (vs 4.70 +- 0.07), m_u_pred = 2.17 MeV (vs 2.16 +- 0.40).",
